the-firm-as-one-program-9 : List Word
the-firm-as-one-program-9 = unlines (cons "- **O6** After what C++ and OCaml are worth: what a language requires to support their desiderata, correctness a large group can rely on and control of the machine." (cons "  - **O6.1** Meaning precise enough to reason about: OCaml's types are the start, dependent types with proofs the end. [P2: Programs, relations and their justifications in one language, with the reasoning kept as data (hyperactivity v31 §1–2)]" (cons "  - **O6.2** Control of the machine as defined meaning: layout, allocation, timing and hardware as definitions with semantics, not escape hatches. [P6: Machines, operating systems and fleets as one program through composed handlers (hyperactivity v31 §7)], [P7: One evaluator realizes everything, through C (hyperactivity v31 §9)]" (cons "  - **O6.3** Staging and specialization in the language itself: templates and HardCaml generators are partial evaluation without a correctness relation; the Futamura projections with proofs are the complete form. [P5: Specialization (the Futamura projections) that keeps its proofs (hyperactivity v31 §6)]" (cons "  - **O6.4** One language across the whole firm: HardCaml shows Jane Street wanting strategy, tooling and circuits in one language. [C1: Prove any provable property of the whole firm ([P2], [P6], [P7])]" (cons "  - **O6.5** End-to-end optimization. [O7: Nothing in computer science is not developed fully here; this was the three-year study of the industry before execution. Optimization, end-to-end optimization]" (cons "  - **O6.6** Jane Street got correctness and is fighting for control; Citadel Securities got control and is fighting for correctness; the cubical core makes both definitions of one language. [P2: Programs, relations and their justifications in one language, with the reasoning kept as data (hyperactivity v31 §1–2)], [P6: Machines, operating systems and fleets as one program through composed handlers (hyperactivity v31 §7)]" nil)))))))
